<title>UK: Heart attacks top world death list, report finds.</title>
<headline>Heart attacks top world death list, report finds.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>A report published on Friday finds that heart attacks and stroke are the leading causes of death worldwide, even in the developing world.</p>
<p>Here is a summary of the main causes of death in 1990 as found in the report, commissioned by the World Bank and carried out with the help of the World Health Organisation.</p>
<p>Rank     Cause			    Number of deaths</p>
<p>	   All causes			 50,467,000</p>
<p> 1	 Heart Disease		     6,260,000</p>
<p> 2	 Stroke				4,381,000</p>
<p> 3	 Pneumonia, lower</p>
<p>	   respiratory infections	  4,299,000</p>
<p> 4	 Diarrhoea			   2,946,000</p>
<p> 5	 Perinatal			   2,443,000</p>
<p> 6	 Chronic lung</p>
<p>	    disease			    2,211,000</p>
<p> 7	 Tuberculosis</p>
<p>	    (non-HIV)			  1,960,000</p>
<p> 8	 Measles			     1,058,000</p>
<p> 9	 Road accidents			999,000</p>
<p>10	 Lung, trachea and</p>
<p>	    bronchial cancer		   945,000</p>
<p>11	 Malaria				856,000</p>
<p>12	 Self-inflicted		     786,000</p>
<p>13	 Liver cirrhosis		    779,000</p>
<p>14	 Stomach cancer		     752,000</p>
<p>15	 Congenital			   589,000</p>
<p>16	 Diabetes			     571,000</p>
<p>17	 Violence			     563,000</p>
<p>18	 Tetanus				542,000</p>
<p>19	 Kidney failure		     536,000</p>
<p>20	 Drowning			     504,000</p>
<p>21	 War injuries			 502,000</p>
<p>22	 Liver cancer			 501,000</p>
<p>23	 Inflammatory heart</p>
<p>	    diseases			     495,000</p>
<p>24	 Colorectal cancer		  472,000</p>
<p>25	 Malnutrition			 372,000</p>
<p>26	 Oesophagus cancer		  358,000</p>
<p>27	 Whooping cough		     347,000</p>
<p>28	 Rheumatic heart</p>
<p>	   disease				340,000</p>
<p>29	 Breast cancer			322,000</p>
<p>30	 HIV/AIDS			     312,000</p>
<p>If all types of cancer are added together, cancer becomes the third leading cause of death worldwide.</p>
